  "brief": "<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Market Overview</h2>\n\nPre-market showing classic risk-off with tech getting hammered (-3.26%) while defensive sectors rally. SPY down 0.93% to $750, but VIX only at 23.84 suggests this isn't panic mode yet. Iran tensions escalating with missile warnings at US warships - geopolitical premium building into Friday's NFP.\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> What to Watch</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Non-Farm Payrolls (12:30 ET):</strong> The big kahuna today. Full employment data dump including wages and participation rate.</li>\n<li><strong>Iran-US Tensions:</strong> Warning missiles fired at US warships in Gulf of Oman. Oil and defense plays getting bid.</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Rotation:</strong> QQQ down nearly 2% pre-market. Watch if this is profit-taking or real distribution.</li>\n<li><strong>G III Apparel (GIII):</strong> BMO earnings with -$0.31 EPS estimate. Consumer discretionary health check.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-amber\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚡ Key Driver</div>Jobs report at 12:30 ET will dictate afternoon direction. Strong number could accelerate tech selling as rate cut hopes fade further.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Sector Rotation</h2>\n\nMoney flooding into defensive plays - Consumer Staples (XLP) up 1.71%, Health (XLV) +1.45%, Utilities (XLU) +0.86%. Classic flight to safety with geopolitical heat and NFP uncertainty. Tech getting destroyed while Dow making records - the rotation to value accelerating.\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-red\"><div class=\"callout-label\">⚠ Bear Case</div>Tech breakdown continues with growth premium collapsing. Iran situation escalates, triggering broader risk-off into the weekend.</div>\n\n<div class=\"callout callout-green\"><div class=\"callout-label\">✦ Bull Case</div>Healthy rotation from overvalued tech to fundamentally sound value plays. Dow leadership suggests institutional money still working.</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"sec-icon\">◆</span> Levels That Matter</h2>\n\n<ul>\n<li><strong>SPY $745:</strong> Key support from May lows. Break here opens $735-740 zone.</li>\n<li><strong>QQQ $720:</strong> Major technical support. Violation signals deeper tech correction.</li>\n<li><strong>VIX $25:</strong> Above this level and we're in real fear territory for weekend holding.</li>\n<li><strong>DIA $520:</strong> Dow strength continuation above this resistance confirms leadership rotation.</li>\n</ul>\n\n<hr>\n<p><em>Not a prediction. A preparation. Make your plan before the bell.</em></p>",
